  "output": "Spec ID: token-efficient-tool-responses-ticket01-spec\nRevision: r38 (document: r38-replacement)\nFindings by ID: C6\n\n**C6 — MAJOR — R6/R7/R10, AC38/AC43, T2/T3. High confidence.**\n\n**Contradiction:** §3 “Critic handoff (r38)” explicitly permits an in-flight commit after empty-namespace retirement to create a fresh namespace with an unusable handle. R10 instead requires `result_namespace_retired` when retirement precedes commit; T2 requires “no retired-namespace resurrection.”\n\n**Cheap false pass:** pause an admitted upstream call before its result exists, retire its empty namespace, then resume it. AC38/43’s empty branch verifies zero effect at retirement but never observes the resumed commit. An implementation can pass that branch, retain orphaned bytes, and return a handle the caller cannot use.\n\n**Evidence:** retirement deletes ownership (`internal/service/projection.go:863–874`) and session mappings (`internal/service/inbound.go:950–966`). Existing admitted execution can subsequently produce its result (`internal/service/direct_execution.go:29–63`). Failed future owner binding does not prevent this retained-state resurrection.\n\n**Closing criterion:** amend AC38/43 in place to observe admitted execution → empty-namespace retirement through the production trigger → resumed over-ceiling result. Require `result_namespace_retired`, no handle, and no retained entry or aggregate increase. The same invariant must survive tombstone clearing. Reconcile the handoff with R10/T2 without weakening their contract.\n\nThis is a **new repair consequence**, not reopening C5: r38 introduced the zero-effect branch and expressly allowed the late commit.\n\n### Verified closures\n\n- **C5’s refusal/discovery contradiction:** closed for retirement itself. A live record releases at least 256 bytes, funding its tombstone without increasing aggregate charge; an empty namespace persists nothing. AC38/43 exclude owner reinjection and deferred discovery records. C6 prevents accepting the complete lifecycle.\n- **AC7 advisory:** closed. Structural enumeration occurs after the sweep hook at the post-clearing clock. Legitimate sweep-driven reclamation passes; surviving empty containers fail.\n- AC15’s entry refusal and AC39’s reservation/marker accounting remain consistent with retirement’s release arithmetic.\n\n### Per-requirement verdicts\n\nR1 PASS; R2 PASS; R3 PASS; R4 PASS;\nR5 PASS; R6 REVISE; R7 REVISE; R8 PASS;\nR9 PASS; R10 REVISE; R11 PASS; R12 PASS;\nR13 PASS; R14 PASS; R15 PASS; R16 PASS.\n\nGolden-byte, invocation-count, reload, precedence and registry oracles address the other reviewed cheap passes. Serialization includes escaping and duplication, excludes JSON-RPC framing; 8192 passes unchanged, 8193 pages. Indices are 1-based; remaining bytes use original serialized bytes; execution error status is preserved.\n\nT1–T5 each name falsifiable checks, but T2/T3’s lifecycle acceptance is incomplete; downstream completion cannot be accepted.\n\n### Coverage and limits\n\nFull candidate, shared risk packet, decisions and r37/r38 observations read. No silent OD1–OD3 resolution found. C6’s late-commit exception weakens a settled invariant; request coordinator escalation to configured `spec_critic_escalated`.\n\nBinary-only checks cannot prove no-remarshal, entropy provenance, physical reclamation or exact internal registries; documentation also needs inspection. §7 binds emission/scraping to AC13/14; collector delivery remains outside local proof (`docs/logging-contract.md:619–630`).\n\nNo writes or tests executed. Supplied hashes were not independently recomputed: no local hashing tool. No execution permission granted.\n\n### Verdict\nREVISE\n",
